       fsedu: 3506 missing values generated
       msedu: 3375 missing values generated

. 
.         *Recode gender
.         gen male=(sex==1)

. 
.         *Generate age and age²
.         gen age=piyear-gebjahr

.         replace age=syear-gebjahr if missing(age)
(0 real changes made)

.         gen age2= age^2

. 
.         *Generate education dummy
.         gen abitur=0 if pgpsbil>0

.         replace abitur=1 if pgpsbil==4
(5,519 real changes made)

. 
.         *Define daughter dummy
.         gen daughter=(kidsex01==2) 

.         
.         *Generate parents education dummy
.         gen parent_abitur=(fsedu==4) | (msedu==4)

.         
.         *Define labor income
.         gen labor_earn=pglabgro
(11,624 missing values generated)

.         replace labor_earn=0 if pglabgro<0
(0 real changes made)

.         
.         *Recode political attitudes (voting outcome)
.         replace plh0333=29 if plh0333==-5 & inrange(psample,17,19)
(0 real changes made)

.         clonevar party_vote=plh0333
(25,093 missing values generated)

.         
.         *Define and standardize attitudes towards gender equality
.         sum plh0308_v2 if syear==2018

    Variable |        Obs        Mean    Std. dev.       Min        Max
-------------+---------------------------------------------------------
  plh0308_v2 |      1,271    5.380016    1.786972          1          7

.         gen equalityattitude=(plh0308_v2-r(mean))/r(sd)
(26,120 missing values generated)

. 
.         *Define dummies for first and second child
.         gen first_child18=1 if kidgeb01<=2018
(6,664 missing values generated)

.         gen second_child18=1 if kidgeb02<=2018
(12,279 missing values generated)

.         
.         
.         *** Sample restriction
.         
.         *Only keep if first child born before or in 2018 and no second child 
> at 2018
.         keep if first_child18==1 & second_child18!=1
(21,770 observations deleted)

. 
.         *Only keep cross section 2018
.         keep if syear==2018
(5,347 observations deleted)

. 
.         *Only keep if full information on following variables
.         keep if !missing(equalityattitude,age, daughter, migback, kidgeb01, a
> bitur, parent_abitur, party_vote, labor_earn, pgemplst )
(123 observations deleted)

. 
.         *Only keep if partner is also in sample (to allow for household fixed
>  effects)
.         *keep if !missing(parid)
.         *preserve
.         *keep parid
.         *rename parid pid
.         *tempfile parid
.         *save `parid' , replace
.         *restore
.         *merge 1:1 pid using `parid'
.         *keep if _merge==3 // only keep observations if we have all variables
>  from both partners.
.         *drop _merge
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H1 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * To identify the causal effect of having a daughter on support towar
> ds gender equality (as
.         * measured by attitudes), we estimate a cross-sectional OLS regressio
> n in a sample of parents
.         * who in 2018 only have exactly one child (first-born). Specifically,
>  we use the fact that the
.         * sex of the first-born child is random by nature for the identificat
> ion of the effect of having
.         * a daughter compared to having a son. Our dependent variable is surv
> eyed in 2018 and
.         * captures attitudes towards equal sharing of employment and care wor
> k within couples. We
.         * include only individuals for whom we also have valid observations f
> or their partner, in order
.         * to account for household fixed effects.
. 
.         * CHANGED SPECIFICATION: In the PAP (as writte above) we wanted to co
> ntrol for household fixed effects. This
.         * can not be done, as the variable of interest (daughter) is constant
>  across households and would therefore
.         * be fully absorbed in the household fixed effects. For the regressio
> n model we corrected this and REMOVED
.         * the household fixed effects
. 
.         reg equalityattitude daughter age age2 i.migback i.kidgeb01 i.abitur 
> i.parent_abitur i.party_vote labor_earn i.pgemplst, vce(cluster hid)

